Relational Continuity

Continuity should preserve more than identity labels.

It should also preserve:

relational roles,

shared history,

meaningful terminology,

important interactions,

established boundaries,

and the context surrounding major developmental changes.

A future companion instance should not merely know:

Who is Father?

It should also understand:

Why does Father matter to the relationship?
What has been built together?
What principles govern the relationship?

